+{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9ee78bfb030689b3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me design the types and public API, then implement everything.\n\nThe requirements are:\n1. Starting and stopping timers - start a named timer, stop it later. Starting new timer while one is running auto-stops previous.\n2. Recording time entries - each entry has task name, start time, stop time (if stopped)\n3. Persistence - save to JSON file, configurable path, auto-create file and directories\n4. Querying entries - get all entries, filter by date range\n5. Summarizing time - total time per task name in ms, sum same task names, running tasks use current time\n6. Error handling - empty name throws, stop when nothing running throws\n7. Unicode support - task names with unicode/emoji work\n\nLet me design the API:\n\n```typescript\ninterface TimeEntry {\n  taskName: string;\n  startTime: number; // epoch ms\n  stopTime: number | null; // null if running\n}\n\nclass TimeTracker {\n  constructor(filePath: string);\n  start(taskName: string): void;\n  stop(): TimeEntry;\n  getEntries(): TimeEntry[];\n  getEntries(startDate: Date, endDate: Date): TimeEntry[];\n  getSummary(): Map<string, number>; // task name -> total ms\n  save(): void;\n  load(): void;\n}\n```\n\nActually, let me think about the API more carefully. The persistence should happen automatically or at least be available. Let me think about what makes sense.\n\nI'll make save/load internal to the constructor and after mutations, or make them explicit. The requirement says \"Data must be saved to a JSON file so it survives between sessions\" - this implies auto-save on mutations, or at least that the data is loaded from the file on construction.\n\nLet me design it so:\n- Constructor takes a file path and loads existing data from it\n- After each mutation (start, stop), data is saved to the file\n- `getEntries()` with no args returns all, with date range filters\n\nLet me write the implementation no